// expect: 42
// A Float POSITIONAL constructor field filled from an unannotated parameter.
// The field type is a fact the ctor scheme proves (MkBox : Float -> Box), so
// `g` must infer Float from its use as MkBox's argument — as a pattern binds a
// sub-pattern to the field type on the read side. Before expect_same chased
// the argument's live binding, a scalar meeting the NBound(TVar(binder))
// reference CLOBBERED the binder: `g` stayed an unresolved var, floored to the
// i32 word, and the f64 call site (0.5 is proven Float) dispatched through an
// all-i32 $ft — `indirect call type mismatch` at run (Hβ.emit.float-evidence-ft,
// the ctor-arg face; root Hβ.infer.expect-same-chases-bound-var). The fixed
// compiler infers `g: Float`, emits an f64 param, and the value round-trips.
//
// Positional-field-specific: the record form `type Box = {value: Float}` with
// `MkBox{value: g}` is IMMUNE (record construction unifies the field via
// RecordSchemeKind, var-on-the-left; the positional path goes through
// infer_call_saturated → expect_same). Distinct ctor name (MkBox != Box) — the
// canonical single-variant ADT, SYNTAX.md's own `type Token = Tok(...)` idiom.
type Box = MkBox(Float)

fn wrap(g) = MkBox(g)

fn main() = match wrap(0.5) {
  MkBox(x) => if x > 0.25 && x < 0.75 { 42 } else { 0 }
}
